# CWS store listing

Official: [Creating a great listing page](https://developer.chrome.com/docs/webstore/best-listing),
[best practices — store listing](https://developer.chrome.com/docs/webstore/best-practices).
Skill + checklists: `.cursor/skills/chrome-web-store-best-practices/`.

Listing is not live yet — optimize for **accurate first publish**, not hype.

## Copy

- **Title:** clear function, concise, unique — no keyword stuffing.
- **Summary:** ≤132 characters; real use case; no “best/fastest” or competitor digs.
- **Description:** overview + short feature bullets; no keyword spam.
- Match shipped behavior and `PRIVACY.md` (no analytics; local rules/storage).

## Images

| Asset | Size |
|-------|------|
| Screenshots | 1280×800 or 640×400; 1–5; full bleed; square corners; no padding |
| Small promo tile | 440×280 |
| Marquee | 1400×560 |

- Sharp, current UI; light text; consistent branding with icon.
- No fake “Editor's Choice” / “#1” claims; avoid busy/white-heavy promos.
- Drafts may exist in `readme-resources/screenshots/` — refresh if UI drifted.

## Category & trust

- Default fit: **Developer Tools** (confirm in dashboard before submit).
- Set homepage + support URLs in the developer dashboard.
- Screenshots/video should teach onboarding before install.

## Do not

- Treat this as Firefox/AMO guidance.
- Contradict privacy-first claims for marketing.
- Invent React/Next.js listing advice.
